eligibility_criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* studies utilizing transcranial focused ultrasound for neuromodulation on humans from 2014 to 2024;

Exclusion Criteria:

* review articles;
* studies not conducted on humans;
* studies focused on ultrasound applications other than brain neuromodulation;
* studies focused on the physical or material properties of ultrasound;
* studies that utilized diagnostic ultrasound, non-focused transcranial ultrasound or transcranial pulse stimulation, which has a shorter pulse duration (a few µs) and a different intensity distribution

Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients who underwent their initial ACLR surgery;
* Studies reporting that undergoing initial ACLR surgery with Local Infiltration Analgesia (LIA) and Femoral Nerve Block (FNB);
* Studies about pain-related outcomes at rest with pain scores (pain scores which reported as verbal, visual or numerical rating scales [Numerical Rating Scale] were all converted to a standardised 0–10 scale, known as visual analog scale [They should have a Visual Analog Scale], in the same way, if using a They should have a Visual Analog Scale of 0–100 mm for pain assessment, it was also converted to a 0–10 scale) [];
* Level 1 RCTs studies.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Non-English articles;
* Level 2–5 evidence studies;
* Studies that examined outcomes in patients treated with combined anesthesia;
* Studies that provided postoperative LIA;
* Studies that did not report results within 24 h after surgery;
* Studies with a sample size of fewer than five patients;
* Studies that had only abstracts but no full texts.

Inclusion Criteria:

* patients with early breast cancer (eBC) with small- to medium- breast size and mild to moderate ptosis;
* patients with a follow-up period ranging from 6 to 18 months (median follow-up 11 months);
* patients who underwent Oncoplastic Breast Surgery (OBS) using an Ultrasound (US)-assisted periareolar approach.

Exclusion Criteria:

* patients with pathological skin involvement;
* tumors located more than 8 cm far from the nipple-areola complex;
* patients with a follow-up period less than 6 months or more than 18 months

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Diagnosis of Myofascial Pain Syndrome (MPS) in the upper trapezius;
2. Presence of active Myofascial Trigger Points (MTrPs) within the upper trapezius identified according to the Simon criteria:
   a. Presence of a palpable taut band in the upper trapezius;
   b. Presence of an excessive MTrPs in the taut band;
   c. Local twitch response elicited by the snapping palpation of the taut band (where palpation is possible);
   d. Referred pain due to MTrPs compression.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Clinical signs of cervical radiculopathy;
2. A history of neck trauma (whiplash, vertebral fractures) or prior cervical surgical interventions;
3. Fibromyalgia syndrome;
4. Coexisting nausea, vomiting, or vertigo;
5. Received therapeutic nerve blocks or botulinum toxin administration within the preceding 12 months.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients with a diagnosis of acute cholecystitis at high surgical risk or deemed unfit for cholecystectomy;
* Systematic reviews and meta-analyses published within the last five years;
* Studies using the keywords: ‘Clinical Utility of Endoscopic Ultrasound-guided gallbladder drainage’, ‘gallbladder drainage’, ‘endoscopic gallbladder drainage’.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Non-English language studies;
* Single case reports or case series with fewer than three patients;
* Narrative reviews, editorials, or letters without original patient data;
* Meta-analyses that did not clearly specify the type of stent used for transmural Clinical Utility of Endoscopic Ultrasound-guided drainage (LAMS, fully covered self-expandable metal stents [FC-SEMS], or other)

Inclusion Criteria:

* Subjects with an onset of idiopathic scoliosis below the age of 10, diagnosed by clinical examination and a standard standing posteroanterior radiograph of the whole spine;
* Received full-time underarm thoracolumbar sacral orthosis bracing treatment until skeletal maturity (advised to wear at least 20 h a day);
* Available clinical data of curve features;
* Longitudinal follow-up every 6 months and past skeletal maturity at last follow-up, which was defined as either ≥2 years post-menarche for girls or <1 cm growth in body height in recent 6 months for both genders for intention-to-treat analysis.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Subjects who did not receive bracing or had a diagnosis of scoliosis with any known etiology, such as congenital scoliosis, neuromuscular scoliosis, scoliosis of metabolic etiology, scoliosis with skeletal dysplasia, known endocrine and connective tissue abnormalities, known heart condition or other diseases that could affect the safety of exercise, eating disorders or gastrointestinal malabsorption disorders and currently taking medication that affects bone or muscle metabolism.
